## https://www.riverbankcomputing.com/pipermail/pyqt/2026-November/046574.html (curl exit 0)
subject: PyQt v6.12.1 Wheels Available for Testing
author:  Veronica Berglyd Olsen 
date:    Sat Nov 14 16:03:37 GMT 2026
body, first lines:
    > The PyQt v6.12.1 wheels are available for testing at the local pypi
    > server. There are .1 releases of all other wheels as well.
    > 
    > Hopefully these resolve all the outstanding issues.
    > 
    > Phil
    > 
    The typing stubs for 6.12.1 now generate a two new errors for me with pyright
    1. For pyqtSignal it gives:
    error: Argument missing for parameter "arguments" (reportCallIssue)
    So arguments is now a required parameter, which it shouldn't be.
    QtCore.pyi:
    class pyqtSignal:
        signatures: tuple[str, ...]
        def __init__(self, *types: typing.Any, name: str = ..., revision: int = ..., arguments: collections.abc.Sequence[str]) -> None: ...
    2. For subclasses of QWidget (at least) it requires that the super is initialised with Self, instead of previous QObject | None, so all  my subclasses require I pass self to the super.
    error: Argument of type "QWidget" cannot be assigned to parameter "parent" of type "Self at _NewProjectForm" in function "__init__"
    QtWidgets.pyi
    class QWidget(QtCore.QObject, QtGui.QPaintDevice):
        class RenderFlag(enum.Flag):
            DrawWindowBackground: QWidget.RenderFlag
            DrawChildren: QWidget.RenderFlag
            IgnoreMask: QWidget.RenderFlag
        def __init__(self, /, parent: typing.Self = ..., flags: QtCore.Qt.WindowType = ...) -> None: ...
    Veronica Berglyd Olsen

## https://www.riverbankcomputing.com/pipermail/pyqt/2026-November/046578.html (curl exit 0)
subject: PyQt6 6.12.1 stubs: typing.Self breaks type checking across all modules
author:  Dragan A. 
date:    Sun Nov 15 23:08:31 GMT 2026
body, first lines:
    Hi Phil,
    Veronica reported two pyright errors with the 6.12.1 stubs
    (https://www.riverbankcomputing.com/pipermail/pyqt/2026-November/046574.html
    ).
    They are not two separate issues. The 6.12.1 stubs replace a class's own
    name with typing.Self everywhere, and in most of those places Self is
    wrong.
    6.12.0 works fine: pyright reports 0 errors in our project. After updating
    to 6.12.1, with no other change, it reports 716 errors in 136 files. For
    example, 6.12.0 has
        QCoreApplication.instance() -> 'QCoreApplication|None'
    where 6.12.1 has
        QCoreApplication.instance() -> typing.Self
    QtCore.pyi in 6.12.0 doesn't use typing.Self at all; in 6.12.1 it
    appears 567 times. The code runs fine on 6.12.1; only the stubs are wrong.
