## https://www.riverbankcomputing.com/pipermail/pyqt/2026-November/046579.html (curl exit 0)
subject: PyQt6 6.12.1 stubs: typing.Self breaks type checking across all modules
author:  Randy Northrup 
date:    Mon Nov 16 00:45:10 GMT 2026
body, first lines:
    Hi Phil,
    Adding to Dragan's and Veronica's reports: mypy shows the same, and a few
    more places where typing.Self doesn't fit.
    With PyQt6 6.12.1, mypy 2.4.1 --strict on this file:
        from PyQt6.QtCore import QObject, pyqtSignal
        class A(QObject):
            changed = pyqtSignal(int)
        class B(QObject):
            def watch(self, a: A) -> None:
                a.installEventFilter(self)
                a.removeEventFilter(self)
                self.setParent(None)
    gives:
        repro.py:5: error: Missing named argument "arguments" for
    "pyqtSignal"  [call-arg]
        repro.py:10: error: Argument 1 to "installEventFilter" of
    "QObject" has incompatible type "B"; expected "A"  [arg-type]
        repro.py:11: error: Argument 1 to "removeEventFilter" of "QObject"
    has incompatible type "B"; expected "A"  [arg-type]
        repro.py:12: error: Argument 1 to "setParent" of "QObject" has
    incompatible type "None"; expected "B"  [arg-type]
    With PyQt6 6.11.0 the same file passes.
    So besides pyqtSignal's "arguments" having no default:
    - QObject.installEventFilter(), removeEventFilter() and setParent() take
      typing.Self where any QObject is meant, and setParent() has also lost
